--- !u!114 &6040056607672438406
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 419825187659857983}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d2e7531c529015f43852996b022e58ba, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialManager
  tutorialPanel: {fileID: 7722570527847296942}
  titleText: {fileID: 389066931245446839}
  explanationText: {fileID: 2992718025034857210}
  pageNumberText: {fileID: 8695806678227050430}
  previousBtn: {fileID: 5898662456294313673}
  nextBtn: {fileID: 7383123004082277708}
  continueBtn: {fileID: 8945789286269889109}
  taskReminderPanel: {fileID: 0}
  taskReminderText: {fileID: 0}
  steps:
  - stepName: MOVEMENT AND CONTROLS
    pages:
    - title: WELCOME TO RUSTCRAVE!
      explanationText: "In this dying mechanical world, you must lead your Swarm
        through collapsing tunnels. \n\nDig for resources, avoid deadly hazards,
        and gather enough power to face the ultimate challenge!\n\nRemember that
        when the screen catches up with the unit and it moves out of the screen boundaries,
        the unit dies!"
    - title: COMMANDING THE SWARM
      explanationText: "Movement and control are the foundation of your survival.
        \n\nTo select a unit, click the Left Mouse Button (LMB) on them in the world,
        click their portrait in the UI, or use the 1-9 shortcuts on your keyboard."
    - title: MOVEMENT
      explanationText: "Once a unit is selected, click the Right Mouse Button (RMB)
        on an empty spot to order them to move there. \n\nKeep moving, or the collapsing
        tunnel will consume you!"
    requiredTask: 1
    taskReminderText: Select your units and move them to the designated area!
  - stepName: INTERACTIONS AND MINING
    pages:
    - title: INTERACTIONS AND COMBAT
      explanationText: "The tunnels are filled with valuable minerals and hostile
        threats! To interact with them, simply select your unit and click RMB on
        the target. \n\nYour units will automatically perform the correct action:
        attacking or mining."
    - title: GATHERING RESOURCES
      explanationText: "Breaking a rock or defending the enemy is only half the job.
        \n\nDropped resources must be collected! Select a unit and click RMB on the
        loose object to pick it up."
    requiredTask: 2
    taskReminderText: Order one of your swarm units to mine a mineral and pick it
      up!
  - stepName: COMBAT
    pages:
    - title: ATTACKING
      explanationText: "The tunnels are filled with valuable minerals and hostile
        threats! To interact with them, simply select your unit and click RMB on
        the target. \n\nYour units will automatically perform the correct action:
        attacking or mining."
    requiredTask: 3
    taskReminderText: Order one of your swarm units to attack and kill enemy!
  - stepName: ROBOTS INFO
    pages:
    - title: UNIT VITALS
      explanationText: "Every robot is driven by specific internal systems. \nKeep
        a close eye on them: \n\nEnergy: Drains passively over time and drops faster
        when acting. If it hits 0, the robot shuts down permanently! \n\nHP (Health):
        Lost in combat or from hazards. If it reaches 0, the robot is destroyed.
        \n\nInventory: Defines how many items a unit can carry before becoming overloaded."
    - title: SWARM CLASSES
      explanationText: "Your robotic companions are specialized for specific tasks
        to optimize Energy usage:\n\nDiggers: Masters of excavation. They consume
        less Energy while mining. \n\nDefenders: Built for combat. They burn less
        Energy during engagements. \n\nSpecialists: Equipped with unique abilities,
        which they cast at a reduced Energy cost.\n\n"
    - title: ABILITIES
      explanationText: "Some robots possess powerful active skills! \nSelect the
        unit and press RMP or Spacebar on them to aim and activate their unique ability
        using RMP again!"
    - title: THE HOLLOW CONDUCTOR
      explanationText: "Your main character, the Conductor, cannot fight or mine
        directly. However, its special ability allows the Spider-Constructor to detach
        from the puppet body! \n\nWhile detached, the Spider can perform basic actions,
        but you lose the ability to command the rest of the Swarm. Use this tool
        wisely!"
    - title: ADVANCED MOVEMENT
      explanationText: "To improve your multitasking, you can move the Conductor
        independently using \u201DWSAD\u201D, and quickly activate its Detachment
        ability by pressing \u201CE\u201D. To go back to your puppet's body just
        press \"E\" again.\n\nRemember that when spider moves out of the screen boundaries
        (either when on the puppet body or on its own) the game instantly ends!"
    requiredTask: 5
    taskReminderText: Press 'E' to detach the Conductor and start digging and attacking
      if neccesary!
  - stepName: FINISH TUNNEL
    pages:
    - title: SURVIVE AND ADAPT
      explanationText: "Excellent! \n\nYou have grasped the core mechanics of survival.
        I won't reveal all the secrets of Aion just yet... \n\nFor now, let's catch
        our breath before the real hunt begins. See you in the Asylum!"
    requiredTask: 6
    taskReminderText: Move all surviving units to the exit zone.
  globalActiveModifier: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d373c29c877b50b43b30a9a517ecce77, type: 2}
  calmModifierData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 069328bb56aa91c4ebe23918f08f63e8, type: 2}
